# Ball Takes UI Rules

- Preserve the black/green Ball Takes identity.
- Treat green as an accent, not a default surface.
- The shell must be clean; football, memes, GIFs and receipts provide the chaos.
- Do not introduce glassmorphism, excessive glow, unnecessary gradients, or generic AI-dashboard styling.
- Prefer whitespace and typography over adding borders around everything.
- Use the existing design system first; consolidate one-off styling into shared tokens/components.
- Do not add arbitrary Tailwind values when an existing token can express the intent.
- Limit each screen to one dominant action and a few secondary focal points.
- Use football visual identity: crests, scorelines, kickoff, matchweek, Aura and pundit comparisons.
- Every asynchronous section must explicitly support loading, loaded, empty and error states.
- Never leave empty advertisement placeholders visible.
- Studio is a primary product destination and must never look like a generic blank AI prompt page.
- Banter content should have multiple visual variants rather than one generic card template.
- Respect accessibility, keyboard/focus states, contrast and reduced motion.
- Validate 375px, 768px and 1440px layouts before declaring UI work complete.
